## Node name corrections (11 October 2026)

The local matrix in Copernicus1.md lines 983 to 1007 uses several names that are not COP types in Houdini 22.0.368; the list below gives the real node to use for each of them (11 October 2026)

- `voronoi` does not exist: use `worleynoise` (outputs dist1, dist2, border, center, id), `cellularnoise` (noise, border, center, id, with Gap and Bevel) or `cellpattern` (adds Random Height, Orient tilt, Density culling and Distort) (11 October 2026)
- `shape` does not exist: use `sdfshape` then `sdftomono`, which is the pairing SideFX gives for the Designer Shape node (11 October 2026)
- `slopeblur` does not exist: the Designer Slope Blur is the Distort by Slope recipe, `slopedir` wired into the dir input of `distort`, with Streak set to Min to erode, Max to roughen edges or Blur to smear (11 October 2026)
- `warp` and `directionalwarp` do not exist: use `distort` with Direction Type Angle or Coordinates, or with a dir input; a Designer multi directional warp becomes two to four `distort` nodes at different angles fed by the same blurred noise on their scale input (11 October 2026)
- `edge_detect` is `edgedetect` (Methods Sobel, Prewitt, Laplacian, Simple, Thresholded Sobel); `transform` is `xform2d`; `ambientocclusion` is `heighttoambientocclusion`; `linear` and gradients are `ramp` (Types Horizontal, Vertical, Radial, Concentric) (11 October 2026)
- There is no highpass node: subtract a `blur` of the signal from the signal with `blend` [Mode Subtract], or keep a radial band with `filterfrequencies` [Frequency, Width, Smooth]; the exact normalization of Frequency is UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)
- Flood fill family: `segmentbyconnectivity` gives the island id and alpha; random value per island is `randommono` with the id wired into its seed input; gradient per island is `uvmapbyid` [Mode UV Map]; bounding box size per island is `uvmapbyid` [Mode Size]; area, minimum and maximum per island come from `statisticsbyid` (11 October 2026)
- Levels is `remap` [Operation Remap]; Histogram Scan is `remap` [Operation Threshold, Width for softness]; Auto Levels is `equalize`; Min Max is `statistics`; Blur HQ is `blur` [Filter Gaussian]; Non Uniform Blur and Directional Blur are `streakblur` [Angle, Length, Mode Blur, Min or Max] or `blur` with an anisotropic Scale Size (11 October 2026)
- Tile Generator is `tilepattern`; Tile Sampler and Splatter are `shapescatter` or `curvescatter`; Make It Tile is `tilepattern` plus `feather` for patterns, or an offset copy by `xform2d` [Border Wrap] mixed through a seam mask for images (11 October 2026)
- clouds_2 and perlin_noise are `fractalnoise`; crystal_1 is `crystalnoise`; cells_1 is `worleynoise` or `cellularnoise` (11 October 2026)

## Measurement toolkit for a height reference (11 October 2026)

These seven measurements are the ones named in every family; run them on a central crop of the reference, after detrending, and record the values in the material readout before building any node (11 October 2026)

- **M0 Prepare**: a photo is not a height map, its luminance mixes albedo and lighting; when only a photo exists, use cues from `neural_layertodepth_moge2` (outputs depth, normal, height; Execution Provider must be CPU on macOS per the SideFX page), from `normaltoheight` [Solver FFT or Poisson, X Borders and Y Borders Periodic] when a normal map exists, and from `neural_layertomask_sam2` to isolate elements; the usefulness of MoGe-2 on flat close-up textures is UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)
- **M0 Detrend**: subtract a wide `blur` (Size about a quarter of the frame) before spectra and autocorrelation, and apply a Hann window in a `wrangle` when the crop is not periodic, otherwise the frame edges add a false cross to the spectrum (11 October 2026)
- **M1 Period and grid**: autocorrelation by Wiener Khinchin, offline as acf = ifft2(abs(fft2(h minus mean)) squared).real, or in COP as `fft` [FFT Direction Forward, Center DC on] > `blend` [Mode Hypot] of real and imaginary > `blend` [Mode Multiply] with itself > `fft` [FFT Direction Inverse] with a `constant` 0 on imaginary; the lag-zero position of the COP result is UNVERIFIED, so check it on a known checkerboard first (11 October 2026)
- **M1 Reading**: take the two shortest non-collinear peak vectors a and b; square grid gives equal lengths at 90 degrees, running bond gives b equal to half of a plus one course, hexagonal packing gives 60 degrees, ripples and corrugation give a single direction; a secondary peak above half of the lag-zero value means a strict lattice, 0.1 to 0.5 a jittered lattice, below 0.1 an aperiodic material (thresholds UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **M2 Joint width**: threshold at the valley of the histogram (Otsu), take the black joint mask, run a distance transform inside it and report width as twice the median distance on its medial axis, then the ratio joint width over lattice pitch; in COP `remap` [Operation Threshold] > `monotosdf` [Iso 0.5] > `statistics` gives the maximum half width only, so the median needs the offline step (11 October 2026)
- **M3 Cross section profile**: average 50 or more profiles taken perpendicular to a joint, crest or ridge aligned with the lattice found in M1, then name the shape: plateau with chamfer, plateau with round arris, cushion, dome, V groove, concave grout, asymmetric sawtooth, cusp from folded noise, sine (11 October 2026)
- **M4 Histogram**: `histogram` [Buckets 256, Minimum 0, Maximum 1] and its counts output; report modality, skewness, kurtosis, spikes at plateau levels and the area fraction below the joint threshold; a pure sine profile gives the U shaped arcsine histogram, a sawtooth gives a flat histogram (11 October 2026)
- **M5 Spectrum slope**: radially averaged power S(k), the mean of abs(F) squared over each annulus, fitted in log log between wavelengths of 4 pixels and a quarter of the frame with lattice peaks excluded; for an isotropic fractional Brownian surface the slope is minus (2H plus 2), and a 1D profile gives minus (2H plus 1) (11 October 2026)
- **M5 Noise mapping**: for an ideal octave sum, H equals minus ln(Roughness) over ln(Lacunarity), so Roughness equals Lacunarity to the power minus H; H 0.8 gives a slope of minus 3.6 and Roughness 0.574 at Lacunarity 2; this mapping is derived and UNVERIFIED against the `fractalnoise` code (11 October 2026)
- **M6 Anisotropy**: structure tensor from `derivative` (outputs dCdx and dCdy) > `wrangle` products Jxx, Jyy, Jxy > `blur` [Size two or three feature sizes]; gradient orientation is half of atan2(2 Jxy, Jxx minus Jyy), features run 90 degrees from it, coherence is sqrt((Jxx minus Jyy) squared plus 4 Jxy squared) over (Jxx plus Jyy); a sweep of `filterfrequencies` [Anisotropy Angle, Width 20, Reflect on] gives the energy per direction; report the dominant angle, the coherence and the number of orientation peaks (1 grain, 2 crosshatch or herringbone, 4 grid) (11 October 2026)
- **M7 Components**: binarize at the median and at Otsu; white mask with `segmentbyconnectivity` [Connectivity Above Threshold, Collapse IDs on], black mask with [Connectivity Below Threshold]; areas per island from `statisticsbyid` (area output) then `histogram`; report count per frame, median area, coefficient of variation (CV), the largest component fraction (above half of its phase means a percolating network) and the aspect ratio from `uvmapbyid` [Mode Size]; merge islands across the frame border when the reference is periodic (11 October 2026)

## Stacking conventions and paid pitfalls (11 October 2026)

- **Order**: macro, then meso, then micro, one named chain per layer, never fibers before the macro form, which is the failure diagnosed in the FiberWood audit of Copernicus1.md line 1501 (11 October 2026)
- **Amplitude budget**: micro relief stays at 5 to 15 percent of the meso relief, the Gnomon rule quoted in Copernicus1.md line 897; macro and meso shares depend on the family and are given per recipe as UNVERIFIED start values (11 October 2026)
- **Combining**: Add superposes relief, Maximum lays solids on a base (stones, stamps, chips), Minimum or Subtract carves (joints, cracks, pits), Multiply masks; the `blend` mode indices measured locally are Add 3, Subtract 4, Multiply 5, Divide 6, Hypot 8, Difference 9, Maximum 12, Minimum 13, consistent with the order of the SideFX page (Copernicus1.md line 1534) (11 October 2026)
- **Zero mean details**: every detail layer added to an existing profile must have zero mean, otherwise the measured profile is counted twice; check the mean of each added layer by exporting it (Copernicus1.md lines 1580 and 1606) (11 October 2026)
- **Profiles**: evaluate fitted profile curves in a `wrangle` (cubic Hermite through the knots) and not in a `remap` ramp, whose quantized table produced 2 to 3 pixel steps that became bands in the normal; normal correlation went from about 0.75 to 0.98 (Copernicus1.md line 1553) (11 October 2026)
- **Remap ramps**: a `remap` ramp must cover the whole input range, beyond Input Max the value failed and drew wide black borders (Copernicus1.md line 1536) (11 October 2026)
- **Wrangle layers**: a COP layer in a `wrangle` is RGBA; read p@C.x, write p@C = set(y, y, y, 1), then `channelextract` before `heighttonormal`, which refuses RGBA; @P runs from minus 1 to 1 with y up, @ix and @iy are pixel indices, bit shift operators are not available (Copernicus1.md lines 1532, 1533, 1555) (11 October 2026)
- **Tile local coordinates**: the uv output of `tilepattern` was not readable as @uv in a wrangle; compute tile-local coordinates from @P (fraction of P times the tile count); each tile spans minus 1 to plus 1 in that output, not minus 0.5 to 0.5 (Copernicus1.md lines 1535 and 1556) (11 October 2026)
- **Joint width in `tilepattern`**: Inset dilates the tile edges by the same amount whatever the width or height of each tile, so it is the constant joint width control; with Inset off faint lines can remain between tiles, which the SideFX page removes by turning Anti-Aliasing off and Shape Edge Filter to 0; brick proportions are not documented for the named bonds, so exact proportions use Custom Pattern [Mode Tile Size, Tile Width, Tile Height] with per-row Offset (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Per-element random**: wire the id into the seed input of `randommono`, otherwise one constant value comes out (Copernicus1.md line 1512); `tilepattern` [Tile Value Set Varying, Variation, Seed] also gives one random value per tile without a second node (11 October 2026)
- **Smooth functions**: VEX smooth(a, b, x) misbehaved when a was above b and darkened the whole map; wrap it so it inverts in that case (Copernicus1.md line 1580); replace a hard maximum of symmetric fields by the smooth maximum log(sum(exp(k g))) over k with k about 45, which removes kinks along the symmetry lines (line 1554) (11 October 2026)
- **Alpha trap**: `blend` [Mode Add] on RGBA inputs whose alpha is 1 averaged instead of adding; keep height layers Mono, or give additive RGBA layers an alpha of 0 (Copernicus1.md line 1561) (11 October 2026)
- **Export**: write heights with `rop_image` [colorconversion raw] as float or 16 bit, a gamma on a height or normal export silently shifts 0.5 to 186 out of 255 (Copernicus1.md line 1515) (11 October 2026)
- **QA only**: `heighttonormal`, `heighttoambientocclusion` and `heighttoshadow` are inspection tools during a height pass; check the Normal Type (Signed or Offset) before reading values, locally the normal came out already encoded 0 to 1 (Copernicus1.md line 1516) (11 October 2026)

## Tileability toolkit (11 October 2026)

- **Noises**: `fractalnoise`, `worleynoise`, `cellularnoise`, `cellpattern`, `crystalnoise`, `bubblenoise`, `phasornoise` and the grunge nodes all expose Tile Size; set it to the canvas and pick element sizes that divide it; the locally measured parm names for the tiling switch and period are dotiled = 1 and tilesizex = 1.0 (Copernicus1.md line 1477) (11 October 2026)
- **Patterns**: in `tilepattern` the Mode menu (Seamless, Tile Count, Tile Size) belongs to Pattern Type Custom Pattern, and the SideFX page states that with Seamless and its Divisions parameter the pattern is always tileable; named bonds (Stack, Stretcher, English, Flemish and the others) take their tile amount from the menu right of Pattern Type, so their seam behaviour must be checked with the half offset test (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Stampers**: `shapescatter` [Do Tiled] snaps the grid to divisors of Stamps X and Stamps Y; `stamppoint`, `curvescatter` and `copyxform` have [Wrap Mode On, Tile Size], and Wrap Mode Auto only wraps when the size_ref border is Wrap (11 October 2026)
- **Filters**: set the layer border to Wrap (glossary: values outside wrap around the boundary) and turn on Read Pixels outside Image on `blur`, `derivative`, `slopedir`, `curvature` and `heighttonormal`, Include Border on `feather`, Border Wrap on `distort`, `streakblur` and `xform2d` (11 October 2026)
- **False friend**: the Tile Size of `idtosdf`, `monotosdf` and `eikonal` is a block size for parallel work that should not change the converged result, it is not a tiling period (SideFX `eikonal` page) (11 October 2026)
- **Simulations**: wrap behaviour of `heightfield_erode`, `heightfield_slump` and the reaction diffusion block is UNVERIFIED; test it, and if seams appear, run the simulation on a 3 by 3 repeat built with `xform2d` [Border Wrap] copies, then crop the centre tile (11 October 2026)
- **Per-element seams**: an element cut by the canvas border must get the same random value on both sides; whether `tilepattern` [Mode Seamless] gives both halves the same id is UNVERIFIED, so when in doubt compute the element index from wrapped coordinates in a `wrangle`, as the local per-tile wrangles do (Copernicus1.md line 1581) (11 October 2026)
- **Check**: offset the result by half a frame with `xform2d` [Translate 0.5 0.5, Border Wrap] and inspect the cross through the centre; numerically, the mean absolute difference across the wrap seam must match the mean difference between neighbouring interior columns (11 October 2026)
- **Reference images**: the reference never needs to tile but the result must; for AI-generated sheets, extract the central cell and mirror it into a symmetric working reference before measuring (Copernicus1.md line 1731) (11 October 2026)

## Group A: Ceramics and tiled surfaces (11 October 2026)

Glazed and unglazed fired clay and the floors that imitate it; the common skeleton is a lattice of flat or domed elements separated by joints, so `tilepattern` or a stamper gives L1 in every family of this group (11 October 2026)

### A1 Glazed ceramic wall tiles (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: a regular grid of square or rectangular tiles, commonly 100 to 200 mm, laid stack bond or running bond for subway tiles, each tile slightly offset in height and tilted relative to its neighbours (lippage); the wall itself is nearly planar (sizes and lippage UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: recessed grout joints of 1.5 to 3 mm, a cushion edge (rounded shoulder) or a rectified sharp edge, and a glaze slightly domed toward the centre of the tile (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: glaze waviness (orange peel), pinholes from bubbles that burst and only partly healed, crawling patches, and crazing on old tiles [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: strict lattice; ACF peaks at (P, 0) and (0, P) with P the tile plus joint pitch and a peak height close to the lag-zero value; running bond gives the oblique pair (P, 0) and (P/2, Q) (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: joint over pitch about 0.01 to 0.03, constant along every line (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: flat or gently domed plateau, rounded shoulders of 1 to 3 mm radius, concave grout 0.5 to 1.5 mm below the face (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: strongly bimodal, a tall narrow face peak widened only by lippage and dome, a small low grout peak whose area fraction is about 2j/P, negative skew (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: discrete harmonics of 1/P along both axes over a weak continuous background steeper than minus 3, glaze being smooth (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: fourfold, orientation peaks at 0 and 90 degrees carried by the joints only; inside a face the coherence is near zero (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: white mask gives one component per tile with CV under 0.05 for machine-made tiles; black mask gives a single joint network percolating in both directions (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED, canvas of 4 by 4 tiles: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, tile field: `tilepattern` [Pattern Type Custom Pattern, Mode Seamless, Divisions 4 for a square grid, or Pattern Type Stretcher Bond with the tile amount menu for subway tiles, Shape Class Basic, Basic Shapes Rectangle, Round Corners 0.02, Inset joint width, Draw As Distance, Fade Distance shoulder width] gives tiles, id and uv; SD: Tile Generator (Pattern Square), or Brick Generator for subway tiles (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, face profile: `wrangle` on the distance output, cubic Hermite shoulder from 0 at the joint edge to 1 at the shoulder width, plus a dome of 0.02 from tile-local coordinates; into H with Maximum over a grout floor at 0.3; SD: Bevel, then Blend Max over a Uniform Color (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, lippage and tilt: `randommono` [Range Values Min/Max, Minimum minus 0.015, Maximum 0.015] with the tile id on seed, into H with Add inside the face mask; tilt with `uvmapbyid` [Mode UV Map, UV Space Image] then a `wrangle` dot(uv, random direction) times 0.01; SD: flood_fill, Flood Fill to Random Grayscale, flood_fill_to_gradient_2 (11 October 2026)
- L4 Meso, grout: concave grout from the joint distance (circular arc 0.5 to 1.5 mm deep, in a `wrangle`) plus `fractalnoise` [Noise Type Perlin, Fractal Type None, Element Size 0.003, Amplitude 0.01] for sand, into H with Minimum inside the joint mask; SD: distance plus perlin_noise, Blend Min (11 October 2026)
- L5 Micro, glaze: `fractalnoise` [Perlin, Element Size about an eighth of a tile, Amplitude 0.003] for orange peel; pinholes from `randommono` [Random per Pixel on] > `remap` [Operation Threshold, Threshold 0.998] > `blur` [Units Pixels, Size 1] subtracted at 0.01 inside faces; SD: perlin_noise plus BnW Spots, Blend Subtract (11 October 2026)
- **Tileable**: Custom Pattern in Mode Seamless with Divisions, Tile Size of every noise equal to the canvas, per-tile random values identical on both halves of a tile cut by the frame (see the Tileability toolkit) (11 October 2026)
- **Pitfalls**: perfectly flat coplanar faces read as CG; a remap ramp for the shoulder bands the normal; a hard maximum between neighbouring tile fields leaves kinks, use the smooth maximum; joints wider than about 4 percent of the pitch read as floor tiles (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Sources**: [S1] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glaze_defects ; [S2] https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/tilepattern.html ; measured lessons in /Users/zenray/.claude/skills/zenray-houdini/Copernicus1.md lines 1528 to 1557 (11 October 2026)

### A2 Painted azulejo tiles with raised glaze lines (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: square glazed tiles in a grid, the design repeating over a block of 2 by 2 or 4 by 4 tiles with mirror symmetry; a tile of about 14 cm is common but the source does not give sizes (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: in arista or cuenca tiles a metal or wooden mould pressed into the unfired clay leaves thin clay ridges that keep neighbouring glaze colours from running together [S1]; in cuerda seca a greasy line mixed with manganese separates water soluble glazes and stays as a dark line between them [S2]; each colour pools as its own puddle (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: crazing of the tin glaze, pinholes, small thickness differences from one glaze colour to the next (UNVERIFIED); some 19th century Porto factories also made high relief tiles in one or two colours [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: two lattices, the tile pitch and the design repeat, which can be a multiple of it; ACF shows both, and mirror symmetry doubles some peaks (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: tile joints of a few mm; relief lines 1 to 2 mm wide that close into curves inside each tile (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: an arista ridge is a narrow rounded bump close to a semicircle; pools are plateaus with a meniscus against the ridge; cuerda seca shows the inverse, a narrow recess between two pools with rounded glaze shoulders (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: multimodal, one level per glaze pool, a small high mode for ridge tops and a low mode for the tile joints (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: broadband from thin curved lines plus the lattice peaks of the tile and design periods (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: globally near zero with fourfold or eightfold symmetry; locally the lines carry a strong tangent orientation (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: a high threshold gives one connected line network per tile; between the lines, pools form components whose areas come in symmetric pairs; the black mask holds the tile joint network (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, tile field: `tilepattern` [Pattern Type Custom Pattern, Mode Seamless, Divisions per design repeat, Rectangle, Inset joint, Draw As Distance]; SD: Tile Generator (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, design lines: draw one quarter of the motif as curves in SOPs, `sopimport` > `rasterizecurves` [Units Pixels, Width 6 to 10, Joints Round, Endpoints Round] > `mirror` [Mode Number and Offset, Number of Planes 2 to 4, Angle 90 or 45] to rebuild the symmetric motif; or compose it from `sdfshape` (Circle with Thickness, Star, Vesica, Polygon) joined by `sdfblend` [Mode Union, Fillet Round] and thinned by `sdfadjust` [Outline]; repeat it per tile with `shapescatter` [Stamps X and Stamps Y equal to the tile counts, Grid Type Grid, Do Tiled on]; SD: Shape plus Tile Sampler, or an SVG node (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, ridge profile: `monotosdf` [Iso 0.5] of the line raster > `wrangle` semicircle h = r times sqrt(1 minus (d over w) squared) for arista, or the inverted narrow recess for cuerda seca; into H with Maximum; SD: distance plus levels, or Bevel (11 October 2026)
- L4 Meso, glaze pools: `segmentbyconnectivity` [Connectivity Below Threshold] on the line mask gives one id per pool > `randommono` [Range Values Specific Values, one level per glaze colour] with the id on seed > meniscus from `idtosdf` and a `wrangle` raise of 0.02 within 1 mm of the walls; into H with Maximum, kept below the ridge tops; SD: flood_fill, Flood Fill to Random Grayscale, then Bevel (11 October 2026)
- L5 Micro, glaze defects: crackle from A3 at a low depth, pinholes as in A1 L5, orange peel `fractalnoise` [Perlin, Amplitude 0.002]; SD: cells_1 borders plus BnW Spots (11 October 2026)
- **Tileable**: tile field in Custom Pattern Mode Seamless; the motif repeats per tile through Do Tiled, and a mirror symmetric motif tiles by construction (11 October 2026)
- **Pitfalls**: painted maiolica carries almost no relief, only arista, cuenca, cuerda seca and tube lining do, so colour boundaries must not become height; lines under 3 pixels give unusable normals; segment pools with Below Threshold so that ridge pixels never join a pool (11 October 2026)
- **Sources**: [S1] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azulejo ; [S2] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuerda_seca (11 October 2026)

### A3 Crackle glaze (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: the underlying tile or vessel is smooth and the crack network covers it uniformly or in zones; deliberate crackle is often strongly accentuated, as in Guan ware [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: a spider web of cracks through the glaze, caused by tensile stress when glaze and body expansions do not fit [S1]; often two generations, large cells subdivided by a finer network (UNVERIFIED); a glaze can craze days or months after firing and craze lines darken with use, which changes albedo and not height [S1] [S2] (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: smooth glaze between cracks; closely spaced craze lines indicate a more stressed glaze than widely spaced ones [S2] (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: none; ACF is a single central peak with at most a faint ring at the mean cell size (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: crack width tiny against the cell size, ratio about 0.005 to 0.02 (UNVERIFIED); in a 2K texture keep cracks at 1.5 to 3 pixels (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: narrow V notch between flat faces, possibly a slight lift of the crack edges (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: one very narrow peak with a thin low tail, strongly negative skew and high kurtosis (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: low energy, almost flat over the band covered by the line network (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: isotropic, slightly curved cracks, first generation meeting at T junctions where new cracks end on older ones (UNVERIFIED for glazes, the T junction rule is read for mud in D3) (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: white cells with a broad, often hierarchical area distribution, CV 0.5 to 1.0; black is one connected crack network (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, base: H from A1 or a `constant` at 0.8; SD: Uniform Color (11 October 2026)
