## Group B: Masonry and paving (11 October 2026)

Units laid in courses or packed in a joint matrix; the bond or packing rule fixes the autocorrelation lattice, and the joint profile fixes the shadow line, so L1 is always the layout and the last layers are always the joint (11 October 2026)

### B1 Brick wall (several bonds) (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: the UK co-ordinating size is 215 x 102.5 x 65 mm with uniform 10 mm beds and perpends, and 215 equals 102.5 + 10 + 102.5 so headers and stretchers bond [S1]; a stretcher face is 215 x 65 mm (pitch 225 x 75) and a header face 102.5 x 65 mm (pitch 112.5 x 75); US modular bricks of about 7.6 x 2.25 in faces with 3/8 in joints are UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)
- **Bonds read in [S1]**: stretcher or running bond staggers each course by half a stretcher; English bond alternates stretching and heading courses with headers centred over stretcher midpoints; Flemish bond puts one stretcher between headers with headers centred over the stretchers below; header bond is all headers offset by half a header; monk bond puts two stretchers between headers centred over the perpend below; English garden wall bond has three stretching courses per heading course (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: per-brick depth offsets and tilts, chipped arrises, slightly bulged or warped faces (UNVERIFIED); mortar joints finished flush, bucket handle (concave), weatherstruck (close to the lower brick and sloping back toward the upper one), recessed (set back flat) or tuckpointed [S2] (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: sand-faced or wire-cut drag marks, pores, mortar sand grain (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: lattice vectors derived from the [S1] sizes: stretcher bond (225, 0) and (112.5, 75); header bond (112.5, 0) and (56.25, 75); English bond (225, 0) and (0, 150); Flemish bond (337.5, 0) and (168.75, 75); monk bond (562.5, 0) and (281.25, 75); stack bond (225, 0) and (0, 75); the ratio of the two lattice lengths identifies the bond before any shape analysis (11 October 2026)
