- **Profile**: flat faces with rounded or chipped arrises of 1 to 3 mm; the joint shows a circular arc (bucket handle), a flat set back floor with sharp brick shoulders (recessed), a slope (weatherstruck) or no step (flush) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: bimodal for recessed and concave joints, with the brick mode near 83 percent of the area; near unimodal for flush joints (derived and UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: strong discrete peaks at the reciprocal lattice of the bond over a background near minus 3 (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: continuous bed joints make horizontal the dominant orientation, perpends are short and staggered (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: white bricks with CV near 0.02 for machine bricks and up to 0.1 for handmade ones; black is one connected mortar network (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
