- **Macro, dry stone**: built course by course without mortar, rows starting with large flattish stones that diminish as the wall rises, through stones spanning both faces and sometimes protruding, hearting packing the voids, a batter that narrows the wall and large cope stones on top; Galloway dykes look porous and rickety with many holes, and smoots are openings up to 200 mm high [S2] (11 October 2026)
