- **Spectrum**: a peak or ring at the stone pitch, then a steep decay near minus 3.5 to minus 4 from the smooth domes (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: rows give one orientation, arcs a rotating one, cobbles none (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: one white component per stone, each containing one local maximum; CV 0.1 to 0.3 for setts and 0.3 to 0.6 for cobbles; black is one connected joint network (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
