## Group E: Wood (11 October 2026)

Fibrous anisotropic material whose height follows the grain; every family here measures a high coherence along the fibres (M6), and most relief comes from a stretched noise warped by a slower field, plus discrete features (knots, checks, plates, lenticels) stamped on top (11 October 2026)

### E1 Bark (several species) (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: the outer bark (rhytidome) is thickest and most distinctive on the trunk and is made of dead cork layers [S1]; trunk curvature does not belong in a tileable height; species differ in kind: furrowed and ridged (oak), plated (pine), smooth with lenticels and peeling sheets (birch, cherry), exfoliating patches (plane), long fibrous strips (stringybark eucalyptus, cedar) (species classes UNVERIFIED, the source does not classify) (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: Pinus thunbergii bark is made of multiple shiny layers, birch bark comes off in long sheets, new lenticels form in the cracks of the cork layers, and cork oak bark can exceed 20 cm in thickness [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: fibres along the trunk, lichen and moss in furrows (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: none; strong vertical elongation for furrowed and plated barks, horizontal elongation of lenticels on birch (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: furrows act as joints between ridges or plates (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: furrowed barks show deep V or U furrows between flat-topped ridges; plated barks show plateaus with stepped layer edges; birch is almost flat with shallow lenticel slits (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: bimodal for deep furrows, narrow with a small negative tail for birch (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: energy concentrated on horizontal frequencies (vertical structures) for oak and pine (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: vertical with high coherence for furrowed barks, horizontal features for birch lenticels (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: pine plates elongated vertically with aspect 1.5 to 3, oak ridges as one connected net, furrows connected along the trunk (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe furrowed (oak)**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, ridge net: `worleynoise` [Element Size the furrow spacing, Element Scale 1 by 5 for vertical stretch, Jitter 1] border > `wrangle` plateau where the border distance exceeds the furrow half width, V or U furrow below; SD: cells_1 stretched, then directionalwarp (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, interlacing and fibre: `distort` [Scale 0.02] by a vertically stretched `fractalnoise` on dir, then `streakblur` [Angle 90, Length 0.05, Mode Blur]; SD: directionalwarp plus non_uniform_blur_grayscale (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, cross cracks on ridge tops: `worleynoise` [Element Scale 3 by 1] border thresholded and masked by the ridge tops, subtracted; SD: cells_1 with histogram_scan (11 October 2026)
- L4 Micro, eroded edges: Distort by Slope [Streak Min] plus a fine vertically stretched `fractalnoise` at 0.03; SD: slope_blur_grayscale_2 and anisotropic noise (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe plated (pine)**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, plates: `grunge_pinebark` [Bark Intensity, Bark Size, Bark Roughness, Element Scale for vertical stretch] as the plate mask, or `cellpattern` [Element Scale 1 by 2, Gap the furrow width, Bevel 0.1, Random Height 0.1, Random Rotation 0.2]; the grunge output is a pattern, so `remap` it into a height before use; SD: cells_1 stretched plus Bevel (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, stacked flakes: per plate, `quantize` [Method Number of Segments, Segments 3 to 5] of a plate-local `fractalnoise`, risers rounded by `blur` [Size 1 pixel]; SD: Quantize Grayscale per plate (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe smooth with lenticels (birch, cherry)**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Meso, base and cracks: `grunge_birchbark` [Base Coverage, Base Sharpness, Lenticels, Lenticel Size, Cracks, Crack Size] as a mask set, remapped to small heights; SD: grunge maps plus gaussian spots (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, lenticels: `shapescatter` [Stretch Mode Variance with Stretch X large so stamps become thin horizontal dashes, Blend Method Minimum for slits or Maximum for raised lips] of `sdfshape` [Vesica] stamps; SD: gaussian spots stretched horizontally (11 October 2026)
