### E3 End grain (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: the grain seen when wood is cut across the growth rings [S1]: a log section, or a grid of end-grain blocks (butcher block, end-grain parquet) whose ring arcs point in random directions (layout UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: concentric growth rings, alternating darker and lighter regions from seasonal growth [S1]; radial checks opening from the pith outward, fine radial rays, the pith at the centre and the bark ring at the edge, circular saw arcs (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: pores of the vessels, in a row in the earlywood of ring-porous woods or evenly spread in diffuse-porous woods (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: a radial quasi-period at the ring spacing, so a ring in the FFT; block layouts add a lattice (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: block joints in end-grain floors, open checks in logs (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: flat when freshly sawn, ring ridges when weathered, wedge-shaped checks that widen outward (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: narrow when sawn, bimodal when the rings are raised (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: a ring at one over the ring spacing (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: locally tangential around the pith, globally weak (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: checks as a few radial elongated black components, pores as many tiny black dots aligned on rings (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Meso, ring field: `uvmap` [UV Space Image] centred on the pith > `uvtopolar` [Angle Units Circles] gives angle and length; a `wrangle` builds rings as frac(length times ring count plus noise), with ring widths varied by a 1D `fractalnoise` read along the radius and the rings bent by a low-frequency `distort`; `ramp` [Type Concentric, Number of Cycles the ring count, Outside Range Repeat] is a faster start; SD: a radial gradient through a Pixel Processor (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, ring profile: asymmetric `wrangle` profile, abrupt at the latewood boundary and gradual through the earlywood (as in E2 L4); SD: a curve on the ring gradient (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, radial checks: in the polar coordinates of L1, a `wrangle` opens a few wedges whose width grows with the radius at random angles; SD: triangle shapes splattered radially (11 October 2026)
- L4 Meso, rays: a faint `phasornoise` or stretched `fractalnoise` along the radial direction from the polar coordinates; SD: directional noise in polar space (11 October 2026)
- L5 Micro, pores: `shapescatter` of tiny dots with the earlywood phase of L1 on its density input for ring-porous wood, Blend Method Minimum; SD: Splatter Circular with a ring mask (11 October 2026)
- L6 Macro, end-grain blocks: `tilepattern` [Pattern Type Stretcher Bond or Custom Pattern grid] where each block moves its pith centre by a `randommono` offset from its id, often outside the block so rings read as arcs; SD: Tile Sampler with a ring image and random rotation and offset (11 October 2026)
- **Tileable**: the block layout tiles; a single log section is not tileable by nature (11 October 2026)
- **Pitfalls**: perfect circles, a constant ring width, checks with identical angles (11 October 2026)
