### E4 Painted wood with peeling paint (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: painted siding or panels; the local reference is lap siding of 8 boards with a wedge per board (Copernicus1.md lines 1348 to 1350 and 1389) (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: paint that builds up to about 1/16 in, roughly 16 to 30 layers, can start cracking and peeling with one more coat; crazing is fine, jagged, interconnected breaks in the top layer; cracking and alligatoring are advanced crazing, cracks first run parallel to the grain and reach bare wood, then form a pattern of horizontal and vertical breaks that looks like reptile skin and flakes badly; peeling to bare wood usually comes from moisture and begins as blisters [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: chalking, a powdering of the paint surface from the disintegration of the resin [S1]; wood fibres in the exposed areas; wrinkling when a top layer dries before the one below [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: the board period from the siding; flakes are aperiodic (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: board seams and the overlap step of the siding (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: a step up from wood to the paint plateau, a raised lip where the paint edge curls, grain grooves in the exposed wood (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: bimodal, a narrow high paint plateau and a broad lower wood mode, plus lip spikes; the local reference was tuned to about 65 percent paint and 35 percent exposed wood (Copernicus1.md line 1357) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: the grain anisotropy plus a broadband from flake edges (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: along the grain; flakes elongated along the grain with an aspect of 2 to 4 (UNVERIFIED); alligatoring adds a weaker perpendicular set [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: white paint as large connected regions with holes; black exposed wood as many patches with a broad size spread, elongated along the grain (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, values quoted from the validated local M_BoisPeintEcaille_01 layers unless marked: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, boards and seams: `ramp` [Type Vertical, Number of Cycles 8, Outside Range Repeat] for the lap wedge, then `distort` [Scale 0.008] by a low-frequency `fractalnoise` for the board wobble (lines 1348 to 1350); SD: gradient_linear_1 repeated, directionalwarp (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, wood substrate: the fibre layer of E2 L3, remapped to minus 0.095 to plus 0.075 (lines 1391 to 1397); SD: anisotropic noise through directionalwarp (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, peel mask: a macro `fractalnoise` (Element Scale 0.45 by 0.22), a stretched `fractalnoise` [Noise Type Worley Cellular F2-F1] and a fine `fractalnoise` (0.04) combined, then `remap` [Operation Threshold] around 0.70 to 0.74 for 65 percent paint (lines 1355 to 1357); a hard threshold after a warp gives angular flakes, a soft one gives round blobs (line 1489); SD: clouds_2 plus cells_1, histogram_scan (11 October 2026)
- L4 Meso, paint plateau: the mask times a plateau of 0.14 into H with Add over the substrate (line 1358); SD: Blend Add (11 October 2026)
- L5 Meso, curled lip: `edgedetect` on the mask > `blur` [Size 2.5 pixels] > `remap` to an amplitude of 0.06 (lines 1360 and 1361); a cleaner variant takes `monotosdf` of the mask and raises only the paint side within a few pixels of the edge; SD: edge_detect then blur_hq_grayscale, or Bevel (11 October 2026)
- L6 Micro, old paint: chalky porosity `fractalnoise` (frequency 0.02) at 0.025 on the paint only (line 1363); alligator cracks from a `worleynoise` border with Element Scale stretched along the grain, inside the paint mask, as thin grooves (UNVERIFIED); SD: clouds_3 or BnW Spots, cells_1 borders (11 October 2026)
- **Tileable**: whole numbers of ramp cycles, Tile Size on every noise, Border Wrap on `distort` (11 October 2026)
