- **Macro, formed**: plywood forms are most commonly 3/4 in or 18 mm thick, modular slab systems use modules no larger than 1 to 2 m, column forms use 20 mm through bolts, wall forms are held by twin steel walers and tie bolts, and board-formed concrete such as the Royal National Theatre carries the impression of the timber shuttering [S1]; panel seams, tie hole grids and board steps make the large-scale pattern (spacings UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
